 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "The vehicle has minor scratches consistent with mileage, most too small to capture in photos. The front-end grille and lower moldings have paint chips, and the grille paint is peeling (see photo). Overall, the paint shows wear consistent with age and mileage. All tires are from the same brand and have appropriate tread depth. All wheels show minimal scratches."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "The seats show light wear consistent with mileage. The driver’s door lower panel has heavy scratches. The inner door panels and interior trim show wear consistent with age and mileage."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "A new transmission and right front axle were installed by Len Stoler Chevrolet at 103,797 miles. The exhaust system shows surface rust but is free of leaks and sounds normal at this time."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "During the road test, the vehicle accelerated, handled, and braked properly. The transmission shifted and operated as designed. No abnormal noise was observed from the wheel bearings or suspension. A scan of the vehicle’s computer system revealed fault codes; further diagnosis is recommended."
  }
 ],
